my name is Margaret Avery and I am the  member for Walden Field ward and the  cabinet member for Communities I was  elected in May 2015 my days are very  flexible and can change at late notice  sometimes I start at 7:00 in the morning  I leave home and I don't arrive back  until late at night the meetings can be  very variable sometimes I can have  meetings all days sometimes I can have  one in the morning one in the afternoon  and one in the evening and that's one of  the things that I enjoy about being in  capsular it's not 9:00 to 5:00 I was  just asked if I would if I would stand I  had to think about it because I was  concerned about time whether I would  like to be pinned down from 9:00 to 5:00  but I was assured it wasn't like that  and I can guarantee it isn't if you are  really interested in democracy then you  should stand to be a counselor it is no  point complaining to account solar water  to your parish to your district to your  County if you have an opinion and you  have never bought  and if you are really serious about  helping others being involved then  standing for council is for you it's 90  years since the act of equal  representation which gave men and women  equal opportunity to vote we are so also  celebrating the hundredth anniversary of  when the first women had the vote next  year we have district council elections  and it would be really good to see more  women coming forward to stand for these  positions there there are always people  who can advise and who can who can help  and if you don't step forward then there  won't be women in politics in the future
 

